Subject: [PATCH] d3d9: keep the declaration-built vertex shader for software-processed vertices

With D3DCREATE_SOFTWARE_VERTEXPROCESSING (or MIXED with software
processing on) the D3D9 runtime transforms and lights the vertices itself
and draws them with DrawPrimitive2: POSITIONT, COLOR0, COLOR1, FOG and the
texture coordinates in its own vertex buffer, with its generated
fixed-function pixel shader and no vertex shader. Two of the UMD's
POSITIONT vertex shader builders matched such a draw. The one built from
the declaration ran first; the one built from the pixel shader's input map
then overwrote its inputs. A ps_2_0 shader declares its inputs by register
(v0, v1, t#), so that map is empty and the vertex shader passed only the
position: every software-processed fixed-function draw lost its colours and
texture coordinates and rendered black, on every host GPU.

The pixel-shader-input builder now runs only when the declaration builder
did not.

Evidence: docs/ffp.md, docs/evidence/ffp/ (src/d3d9_ffp.cpp, --swvp).
Origin: vmlab-win3d ffp worker.
---
diff --git a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/D3D9Draw.cpp b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/D3D9Draw.cpp
index 4069ec6..7d4272e 100644
--- a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/D3D9Draw.cpp
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/D3D9Draw.cpp
@@ -2797,7 +2797,8 @@ D3D9DrawDiffuse(D3D9Device *device, D3DPRIMITIVETYPE primitive_type,
       D3D9InitPositionTDiffuseFixedFunctionVsInfo(&fixed_function_vs_shader);
    const bool generate_position_t_runtime_processed_vs =
       runtime_transformed_vertices && D3D9ActiveVertexDeclHasPositionT(device) &&
-      !generate_position_t_runtime_processed_diffuse_vs && translated_ps &&
+      !generate_position_t_runtime_processed_diffuse_vs &&
+      !generate_position_t_runtime_ps_vs && translated_ps &&
       D3D9InitPositionTPsInputFixedFunctionVsInfo(&fixed_function_vs_shader,
                                                   current_ps);
    /*
